# Can I retire in Argentina as a U.S. veteran?

Yes. A U.S. veteran can move to Argentina and, if eligible for an immigration category, establish legal residence. You do not have to be a military retiree to consider it. But your service record alone does not give you a residence permit, and a monthly VA payment does not automatically establish eligibility.

There are three questions to work through: can your income support the life you want, does your situation qualify for Argentine residency, and could you eventually meet the separate requirements for citizenship?

The answers depend on what you receive, how it is documented, and how you intend to live here. Someone receiving military retirement pay has a different file from someone living on VA disability compensation. A veteran moving with children has different planning needs from someone dividing the year between Argentina and the United States.

